     "title": "7 PIO instructions",
     "text": "<b>set pindirs, 1</b> · <b>set pindirs, 0</b> · <b>in pins, 1</b> and 4 nop. 163 cycles a sample, 32 samples to a word."
    }
   ],
   "say": [
    {
     "at": 0.8,
     "text": "There is another way to make the high level. The pin makes it itself, for an instant, only while it listens, and then looks at what the device does with it."
    },
    {
     "at": 13.26,
     "text": "The pad drives the wire high for 100 nanoseconds. That charges the capacitance of the wire and the device's input to 3.3 volts."
    },
    {
     "at": 23.56,
     "text": "Then the pad lets go. The charge drains through the device's 3 kilohm pull-down, and the voltage falls with a time constant of 216 nanoseconds."
    },
    {
     "at": 35.06,
     "text": "113 nanoseconds after the release, the pad samples the wire. It still holds 1.9 volts: a high."
    },
    {
     "at": 42.92,
     "text": "When the device pulls low, the picture changes. The pad lifts the wire only part of the way, and 10 nanoseconds after the release the wire is back at ground. The sample reads low."
    },
    {
     "at": 57.08,
     "text": "One precharge, one sample, every 1,087 nanoseconds. A second state machine of the RP2350's programmable I O does it in 7 instructions."
    }
   ]
